#: src/frontend/dockwidgets/HistogramDock.cpp:277
#, kde-format
msgid ""
"Method used to determine the number of bins <i>k</i> and their width <i>h</"
"i> for <i>n</i> values:<ul><li>By Number - the number of bins is specified "
"manually</li><li>By Width - the number of bins is calculated based on the "
"specified bin width via <i>k = (max(x) - min(x) / h</i>)</li><li>Square-root "
"- <i>k = sqrt(n)</i></li><li>Rice -  <i>k = 2 * pow(n, 3/2)</i>, simpler "
"alternative to Sturges' method</li><li>Sturges - <i>k = log2(n) + 1</i>, "
"assumes an approximately normal distribution</li><li>Doane - modified "
"version of Sturges' method, see the documentation for more details</"
"li><li>Scott - <i>h = 3.49 * sigma / pow(n, 3/2)</i>, optimal method for "
"normally distributed data</li></ul>"
msgstr "Method used to determine the 数値 of bins <i>k</i> and their 幅 <i>h</i> for <i>n</i> values:<ul><li>By 数値 - the 数値 of bins is specified manually</li><li>By 幅 - the 数値 of bins is calculated based on the specified bin 幅 via <i>k = (max(x) - min(x) / h</i>)</li><li>Square-root - <i>k = sqrt(n)</i></li><li>Rice -  <i>k = 2 * pow(n, 3/2)</i>, simpler alternative to Sturges' method</li><li>Sturges - <i>k = log2(n) + 1</i>, assumes an approximately normal distribution</li><li>Doane - modified version of Sturges' method, see the documentation for more details</li><li>Scott - <i>h = 3.49 * sigma / pow(n, 3/2)</i>, optimal method for normally distributed data</li></ul>"

#: src/frontend/dockwidgets/HistogramDock.cpp:290
#, kde-format
msgid ""
"Use 'Auto' to automatically determine the minimal and maximal values of the "
"data to be used to calculate the histogram. Specify the values manually, "
"otherwise.<br><br><b>Note:</b> any samples which fall on the upper end of "
"the histogram are excluded. If you want to include these values for the last "
"bin you will need to add an extra bin to your histogram."
msgstr "Use 'Auto' to automatically determine the minimal and maximal 値 of the データ to be used to calculate the histogram. Specify the 値 manually, otherwise.<br><br><b>Note:</b> any samples which fall on the upper end of the histogram are excluded. If you want to include these 値 for the last bin you will need to add an extra bin to your histogram."

